WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.620
Sons of Anarchy ran from 2008 through 2014,
and Charlie Hunnam remained an audience favorite

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.660
throughout the entire run.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.000
But what happened to him after the last episode?

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.760
It seems like Hunnam hasn’t been quite the
same since Sons of Anarchy ended.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.340
Moving on from a role after a beloved TV shows
ends is never easy for an actor, especially

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.570
when they've been playing that character for
several years.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.140
For Hunnam, saying goodbye to Jax Teller was
difficult.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.290
In fact, the way he describes the experience
makes it sound as though he went through a

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.580
bit of a grieving process.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.140
Hunnam was overwhelmingly nostalgic for his
time on Sons of Anarchy, and he admitted that

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.830
he would make up excuses to visit the set
and relive his days on the show.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:36.540
He told Glamour,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.440
"I knew the security guards and for a couple
of days said, 'Oh, I forgot something.'

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.150
So they'd let me onto the set, and I'd just
walk around at night because I wanted to be

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.730
in that environment and go through a personal
process of saying goodbye."

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.350
For six years, Hunnam knew that he had a secure
paycheck as Jax Teller.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.530
But once the show finished its run, he was
responsible for making big decisions about

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:00.460
his next career-defining move, and he felt
very intimidated by the process.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.140
Hunnam says that he struggles with insecurity
when it comes to maintaining a career as an

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:04.640
actor.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.700
He told The Talks,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.500
"It's a tricky thing to quantify one's career
because in some ways I am in a position where

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.000
I want to be, I am getting to work with good
directors and tell interesting stories…

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.010
But I always feel like I am one failed movie
away from being unemployable."

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.120
"Here we go, we can only f--- it up from here
on out."

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.640
Hunnam isn't a fan of the process of choosing
roles, and he doesn't enjoy feeling the pressure

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.900
to succeed at the box office every time.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.500
It's no secret that Hunnam is well known for
his good looks.

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:36.380
But he's an actor at heart, not a model, and
he wants to earn respect and attention for

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:36.880
his talents.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.440
He became uncomfortable with the way some
people perceived him during his time on Sons

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.660
of Anarchy — as someone who coasted to fame
on physical appearance alone.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.600
When it comes to how other people see him,
Hunnam told InStyle,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.720
"I try not to think about that too much because
I'm just attempting to shape my own perception

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:54.340
of myself and feel confident in my own identity."

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.540
Hunnam then admitted there will always be
people who see him as just the, quote, "pretty

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:01.320
boy," but despite the stigma, he still wants
to face the challenge of making each and every

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.320
performance work to the best of his ability.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.580
When Hunnam was young, he lived in a rough
neighborhood, so he always had to know how

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:08.300
to defend himself.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.210
And when he signed on to the film King Arthur:
Legend of the Sword, he had to go through

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:15.760
an intense training regimen, which included
learning Brazilian jiu-jitsu.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:20.500
Hunnam ended up getting super into the sport,
and he started feeling the benefits of consistent

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.000
practice.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.700
In fact, he says that jiu-jitsu changed his
mindset.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.500
He told Men's Health,

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.900
"It's not even as much the physical benefit
of training; it's the mental.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.700
When you're training every day in a combat
discipline, it just gives you that eye of

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:32.200
the tiger."

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:36.900
Even after shooting for King Arthur ended,
Hunnam stuck with jiu-jitsu and earned his

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:38.380
blue belt in 2018.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.160
Hunnam's new hobby seems to have had a profound
impact on him.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.620
After all, he doesn't do anything halfway
— and it's probably a good idea for everyone

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.040
to stay on his good side now.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:51.620
Hunnam doesn't think that fame and wealth
are necessarily indicators of success.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.100
He says he actually prefers to work on smaller
projects with less financial backing because

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.460
he feels like the director has more creative
control in that scenario.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:03.900
As opposed to focusing on accolades and high
salaries, he says he just wants to challenge

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.920
himself, create films that he's proud of,
and work alongside directors who have interesting

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.420
ideas.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.780
He told Uproxx,

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:14.260
"If I'm involved in a project that I feel
excited about and it gives me a sense of purpose,

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:18.380
and it gives me a sense of creative fulfillment,
that is deep fulfillment to me, and it evens

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.880
out the balance for me in my own journey.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.220
My success, for me, is about getting to continue
to work on things that make me excited."

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.560
It seems like Hunnam has had a lot to reflect
on since Sons of Anarchy ended, and he's confident

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.080
about the direction he's going in now.

